---
source: misc/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"blkid\")"
---
Locate or print block device attributes (LABEL, UUID, PARTLABEL, PARTUUID, ID).

Lookups and listings use the udev symlinks in /dev/disk/by-*. Probing devices for filesystem
signatures (-p, --probe) is not implemented yet. Commands that need it exit with an error rather
than return incomplete data. Use upstream blkid for probing.

Usage: blkid [OPTIONS] [DEVICES]...

Arguments:
  [DEVICES]...
          Devices to print attributes for. With none, every device that udev knows about is listed

Options:
  -L, --label <LABEL>
          Look up the device that uses this filesystem label

  -U, --uuid <UUID>
          Look up the device with this UUID

  -o, --output <FORMAT>
          Output format: full (the default), value, device or export
          
          [default: full]

  -l, --list-one
          Only print the first match for -L / -U

  -d, --no-encoding
          Don't encode non-printing characters. This has no effect yet, but is accepted for
          compatibility

  -c, --cache-file <FILE>
          Cache file. Ignored, since the udev symlinks are read directly

  -p, --probe
          Probe the device directly (not implemented yet)

  -i, --info
          Print information about probing (not implemented yet)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
